      "lander_must_differ_from_author": false,
      "source": "CA-SEAL2 Astra A02 adjudication (lead, 07:35Z): my Astra brief added \"a lander who could also be the author or a fix worker\" as a break target, which goes beyond the approved model. CA-SEAL's approved B' contract (pm7-build 01:27Z) records author and actual lander in the receipt and bars both, plus the lead and every fix worker, from APPLYING THE SEAL; it does not require the lander to differ from the author. CA-SEAL2 follows that narrower separation; the change record must say so explicitly. In practice the lander is the stream lead's landing step (not the author), and the seal applier is a separate assignee. No frozen-code change for this."
    },
    {
      "finding": "CA2-N01",
      "status": "recorded",
      "binding_order_exact": "CA-SEAL/CA-SEAL2 landing order (Astra N01, binding): (1) finalize CA-SEAL's receipt with the actual lander against the third validator 319f6bff; (2) apply CA-SEAL2's code; (3) finalize the fourth receipt against the fourth validator and the finalized third receipt; (4) claude-projects-refresh adds both exact Spec Lock entries; all in one reviewed landing. Running both writers on an assembled fourth-validator tree re-stamps the third receipt and must not happen."
    }
